WEBVTT

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:42.150
Say...

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:47.700
Could you stop having every 
character start off hungry?

00:01:47.900 --> 00:01:53.320
You're the same as the other new artists.

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.000
A hungry hero who saves

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:58.710
the village from the bad 
guys because they fed him.

00:01:58.970 --> 00:02:02.270
Just like Zuffy from One Park.

00:02:02.270 --> 00:02:04.700
I understand that you like One Park.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.900
That doesn't make it okay to copy ideas.

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:10.080
I wouldn't mind so much if you had an

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:12.510
original approach to the hungry hero.

00:02:12.510 --> 00:02:15.960
But it's clear that you're 
borrowing elements

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.040
from many other series.

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:22.070
Are you drawing manga to 
express someone's ideas?

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:26.720
Didn't you become a manga artist 
to express your own ideas?

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.740
In that case, you need to pour 
your soul into every page.

00:02:30.740 --> 00:02:34.240
Put your life into your work!

00:02:39.760 --> 00:02:42.340
Jellybeans Vanguard Honda.

00:02:42.340 --> 00:02:44.620
I'm in my fifth year as a Jump editor.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.210
I am very worried.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:50.650
I have been assigned to the evil

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.540
which threatens to consume Jump,

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:55.140
Gintaman, designated by the 
Bakufu as a harmful manga.

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:59.470
Gintaman has managed to 
last for eight years,

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:04.290
but in reality, it's just 
the scribblings of a gorilla

00:03:04.290 --> 00:03:07.150
that has the backing of 
animal rights activists.

00:03:08.130 --> 00:03:09.470
Look at the editors.

00:03:09.470 --> 00:03:10.920
The first editor, Konishi,

00:03:10.920 --> 00:03:15.160
ended up unable to say 
anything but "Holy Cow!"

00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:19.200
Holy cow!

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:22.380
The second editor, Daito,

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:27.100
messed up his Samurai 
Commando Mission 1549 date,

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:31.680
so he turned to the world of 
anime and never looked back.

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:33.680
Strategy for survival!

00:03:34.770 --> 00:03:37.380
The third editor, elite Nakasaki,

00:03:37.380 --> 00:03:42.920
hurt his back at a party by 
getting a little too elite.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:47.690
After enduring the hell 
of strict deadlines,

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:49.890
they all snapped.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:54.000
They are all kept in the 
gorilla sanctuary now.

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:55.540
Holy cow!

00:03:55.030 --> 00:03:57.660
Please! Let me watch Madoka Magica!

00:03:57.930 --> 00:03:59.650
I'm elite!

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.710
I'm not like them!

00:04:01.960 --> 00:04:03.990
My assignment to Gintaman was

00:04:03.990 --> 00:04:07.710
essentially a death sentence.

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.200
I heard that Vanguard's 
been sent to Gintaman.

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.820
He just got married.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:15.090
Poor guy.

00:04:15.600 --> 00:04:18.280
I need to find a way to save my neck.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.610
That means I have to discover a new artist

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:25.230
so I can be moved off Gintaman.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:29.730
I've spent days searching 
for an artist with promise,

00:04:29.730 --> 00:04:34.740
but the manga they drew 
was only manga in name.

00:04:35.550 --> 00:04:38.160
Isn't there anyone out there

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.100
who's willing to pour their own words,

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:43.000
their own thoughts, their 
own life into their work?

00:04:44.540 --> 00:04:46.570
Is there anyone out there

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:49.150
to save me from my death,

00:04:49.150 --> 00:04:50.870
to save me from this dark prison?

00:04:50.870 --> 00:04:51.770
...guard-san.

00:04:52.100 --> 00:04:53.340
Vanguard-san.

00:04:53.630 --> 00:04:54.840
Vanguard-san!

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.060
Oh, yes.

00:04:56.060 --> 00:05:00.630
Vanguard-san, someone named 
N3016 is here to see you.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.970
O-Oh, let him in.

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:03.810
Yes.

00:05:05.300 --> 00:05:07.520
N3016?

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:10.740
Oh, it's the guy who drew that

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.430
juvenile crap for the Treasure award.

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:14.220
Today is his first visit.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:16.460
Even his pen name is juvenile.

00:05:17.220 --> 00:05:18.010
Excuse us!

00:05:18.010 --> 00:05:18.530
Hm?

00:05:22.880 --> 00:05:24.970
N3016, get in here!

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:30.310
I am prisoner number 3016.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:33.430
It is a pleasure to meet you.

00:05:36.840 --> 00:05:42.850
<b>Draw Your Life on the Canvas We Call Manga</b>

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.850
They brought me a real prisoner?!

00:05:47.010 --> 00:05:49.830
Instead of throwing me into prison,

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:52.610
they brought a prisoner to me!

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:54.870
N-Nobody warned me about this!

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:57.160
You've got 20 minutes.

00:05:57.160 --> 00:05:58.880
Any longer, and you'll be considered

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:00.520
a fugitive and shot on sight.

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:03.300
Why did he bring all these guards with him

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.370
here to show me his manga?!

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:08.540
And it sounds like he did 
something really bad!

00:06:08.950 --> 00:06:14.110
Uh, I believe that we 
spoke on the phone before

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:16.380
when I was a finalist 
for the Treasure award.

00:06:16.800 --> 00:06:18.060
Do you remember my manga

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:20.880
about a Soul Reaper appearing 
before a prisoner

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:21.870
who's about to kill himself?

00:06:21.870 --> 00:06:23.670
It was nonfiction?!

00:06:23.670 --> 00:06:26.140
We chose a complete 
psycho to be a finalist!

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:29.650
So I wanted to come see 
you in person today.

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:34.480
Drop the weapon, Shachi!

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.850
It's just a pen!

00:06:35.850 --> 00:06:38.450
A pen can be used as a weapon! Drop it now!

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:40.420
I-I can't do that!

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.050
I'm... I'm gonna become a manga artist!

00:06:43.050 --> 00:06:44.210
I'll wait three seconds!

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:44.950
One! Two!

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:45.700
Three!

00:06:45.700 --> 00:06:47.100
Shut up!

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:49.790
What?! What now?!

00:06:49.790 --> 00:06:50.300
Bro!

00:06:50.300 --> 00:06:51.610
Sakata-san!

00:06:51.610 --> 00:06:54.550
Why are you so scared of 
a prisoner in handcuffs?

00:06:54.950 --> 00:06:55.880
Forget it.

00:06:55.880 --> 00:06:57.200
I'll keep an eye on him,

00:06:57.200 --> 00:06:58.480
so scram.

00:06:58.480 --> 00:07:00.550
If Sakata-san is here, 
everything will be fine.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:03.700
Then we'll be having tea at Renoir.

00:07:04.520 --> 00:07:06.830
Sorry about all the fuss.

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:08.220
What took you so long, Bro?!

00:07:08.220 --> 00:07:09.710
I was getting nervous.

00:07:09.710 --> 00:07:11.560
There's another weirdo here.

00:07:11.810 --> 00:07:13.450
Sorry about the late introduction.

00:07:13.450 --> 00:07:17.110
I am prisoner number 4264, the artist.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:20.570
I am number 3016, the writer.

00:07:21.230 --> 00:07:24.420
Together, we are Mute Ashirogi.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:25.900
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:07:25.900 --> 00:07:27.830
Is this Bakuman?!

00:07:28.310 --> 00:07:31.390
U-Uh, so the two of you work together?

00:07:31.390 --> 00:07:34.020
He used to do everything himself.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:35.710
But he was only a finalist, right?

00:07:36.050 --> 00:07:39.030
I happened to be in the same 
prison as him for a short period,

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:43.090
and he wanted the opinion of 
a twenty-year Jump reader.

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:44.690
The art is too dated.

00:07:44.690 --> 00:07:46.350
What?! That's not true!

00:07:46.580 --> 00:07:48.950
Kids are sensitive to that stuff.

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:50.920
Then you draw it!

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:53.330
So we ended up

00:07:55.350 --> 00:07:57.370
working together.

00:07:57.370 --> 00:08:00.240
A manga duo that met in a prison!

00:08:00.350 --> 00:08:02.120
I see...

00:08:02.120 --> 00:08:05.670
These dangerous criminals 
can't draw shounen manga!

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:09.690
We fixed the issues you 
mentioned in our phone call,

00:08:09.690 --> 00:08:11.370
so could you take a look?

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:12.660
Oh shit.

00:08:12.660 --> 00:08:16.050
What will happen to me if 
I say something is bad?

00:08:15.710 --> 00:08:19.210
<b>Revised Edition Ver 1.12
Mute Ashirogi</b>

00:08:16.000 --> 00:08:19.590
Quick! Get this over with and leave!

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:23.350
I'll try to give them advice 
without antagonizing them...

00:08:23.350 --> 00:08:24.590
So...

00:08:24.690 --> 00:08:26.380
The original manga was a touching story

00:08:26.380 --> 00:08:29.050
about a Soul Reaper appearing before 
a prisoner about to kill himself

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:31.840
and using death to teach the prisoner about

00:08:31.840 --> 00:08:33.520
the importance of life.

00:08:33.520 --> 00:08:35.360
The story was too gloomy,

00:08:35.360 --> 00:08:39.730
and everyone had their sleeves ripped off.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:43.420
He was told to draw something 
that wasn't so dark.

00:08:45.230 --> 00:08:46.430
So we

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:47.530
changed things up.

00:08:47.920 --> 00:08:52.540
You just put shoulder pads 
on all of the characters!

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:55.380
And we changed two of the key characters,

00:08:55.380 --> 00:08:57.410
such as the Soul Reaper and 
the warden, into girls,

00:08:57.410 --> 00:08:59.440
so now you have two heroines.

00:08:59.440 --> 00:09:01.370
The heroines are damn scary!

00:09:01.670 --> 00:09:03.930
And they have double shoulder pads!

00:09:03.930 --> 00:09:06.550
Are the shoulder pads the heroines?!

00:09:07.060 --> 00:09:08.320
The main character was thrown

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:11.320
in a women's prison for 
some unknown reason,

00:09:11.320 --> 00:09:13.100
and now he spends his days

00:09:13.100 --> 00:09:15.920
surrounded by the prison ladies.

00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:18.140
These days, Jump doesn't have

00:09:18.140 --> 00:09:20.980
any series that make the readers hard.

00:09:20.980 --> 00:09:24.320
Pretty sure you've only 
made their shoulders hard.

00:09:24.320 --> 00:09:27.000
S-So this is a prison harem story?

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.270
That's new.

00:09:28.270 --> 00:09:29.080
Right?

00:09:29.080 --> 00:09:30.330
We did it, Bro!

00:09:30.580 --> 00:09:35.240
But, Jump is aimed at grade 
school and middle school boys,

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.330
and we don't want them 
sympathizing with prisoners...

00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:39.990
You got a problem with prisoners?!

00:09:39.990 --> 00:09:43.280
We're all prisoners of society!

00:09:43.790 --> 00:09:46.890
I'm busting my ass drawing manga here!

00:09:46.890 --> 00:09:49.490
I spend all of the little time I have left

00:09:49.470 --> 00:09:51.930
after slaving away for hours 
on the chain gang on manga!

00:09:52.170 --> 00:09:54.300
Calm down, N3016.

00:09:54.680 --> 00:09:57.810
Vanguard-san knows that.

00:09:58.250 --> 00:09:59.690
However, we can't create a new

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:01.810
romantic comedy if you 
oppose the prison setting.

00:10:01.810 --> 00:10:04.100
Then you would only have 
school romantic comedies.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:06.950
The prison is what makes 
this manga stand out.

00:10:06.950 --> 00:10:08.560
We can't give that up.

00:10:08.560 --> 00:10:11.270
But we can add some wardrobe malfunctions

00:10:11.270 --> 00:10:12.940
to keep the kiddies happy.

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:15.490
Oh, no! My shoulder pads fell off!

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:18.080
Who gives a damn about 
shoulder pads falling off?!

00:10:18.510 --> 00:10:20.610
And we'll follow Yabuki's example 
with the tankoban releases

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:22.870
by adding detail to the shoulder pads

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:25.870
and showing how tightly 
they adhere to the skin.

00:10:25.870 --> 00:10:28.050
Forget that! Get rid of the shoulder pads!

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:30.340
And this will never make 
it to a tankoban release!

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:32.020
But if you want to do

00:10:32.020 --> 00:10:34.350
a romantic comedy, the art 
needs a little work...

00:10:34.520 --> 00:10:39.350
The girls are just a little 
too beefy, I think.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:44.110
Yeah, Bro's art is too animated 
for a romantic comedy.

00:10:44.110 --> 00:10:46.650
I'd say his art is too 
crappy for a manga artist!

00:10:46.950 --> 00:10:51.590
Really? Maybe it's because I'm 
a fan of the older Jump style.

00:10:51.590 --> 00:10:55.370
Maybe a different pen would help?

00:10:55.370 --> 00:10:56.620
No, it's not that.

00:10:56.620 --> 00:10:58.910
The shoulder pads are a big problem.

00:10:59.810 --> 00:11:01.430
Uh, I believe you should

00:11:01.430 --> 00:11:04.520
completely start over with 
the female characters.

00:11:04.520 --> 00:11:06.340
Do you have any concept 
art for the heroines?

00:11:06.890 --> 00:11:09.360
Oh, I sure do.

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:12.710
This is more like concept 
art for the shoulder pads!

00:11:13.090 --> 00:11:14.610
Right Wing 1.

00:11:14.610 --> 00:11:17.500
Stores a carbon whip that 
shuts up any noisy kid.

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:19.890
Can cow any rowdy prisoner.

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:21.100
Storage?

00:11:21.100 --> 00:11:23.080
These shoulder pads are used for storage?!

00:11:23.600 --> 00:11:24.820
Right Wing 2.

00:11:24.820 --> 00:11:26.440
Armed with an auto-turret that will

00:11:26.440 --> 00:11:29.040
clear any enemies on your right side.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:31.570
Of course. It only hits 
enemies on the right side.

00:11:31.570 --> 00:11:34.060
It's on her right, so it only 
works on the right side!

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:35.830
Left Wing 1.

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:37.520
Stores an extremely powerful stun gun

00:11:37.520 --> 00:11:39.280
that can instantly knock out an elephant.

00:11:39.280 --> 00:11:41.210
And now for the Left Wing 2!

00:11:41.210 --> 00:11:43.160
Hidden?! It was hidden?!

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:45.810
The warden is still a girl.

00:11:45.810 --> 00:11:47.390
She uses this hairbrush 
to take care of her hair.

00:11:47.390 --> 00:11:49.490
Now we find out she's 
actually fashion conscious!

00:11:49.490 --> 00:11:51.570
Of course! She's still a girl!

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:54.060
And the shoulder pads can be removed.

00:11:54.060 --> 00:11:55.480
Metamorphosis?

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:57.770
How much time did you spend 
on the shoulder pads?!

00:11:57.770 --> 00:12:00.170
Why are these shoulder pads 
starting to resemble the Cloths?!

00:12:00.170 --> 00:12:02.010
Isn't this supposed to 
be a romantic comedy?!

00:12:02.010 --> 00:12:05.940
Since this is a Jump manga, we 
wanted to incorporate battles.

00:12:06.730 --> 00:12:08.790
Now take the Soul Reaper heroine.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.680
What are Zanpakupads?

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:11.990
Right Wing.

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:14.510
A strange blade which grows in parallel 
to the user's spiritual power.

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:15.910
Vital for every Soul Reaper.

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:17.230
Left Wing.

00:12:17.230 --> 00:12:19.790
Used for draining spiritual 
power when you're running low.

00:12:19.790 --> 00:12:23.210
You guys are ripping off everything 
under the sun with your shoulder pads!

00:12:23.480 --> 00:12:24.450
Wh-What am I supposed to do...

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:26.690
What's wrong?

00:12:26.690 --> 00:12:28.490
Do you want me to make my 
art look worse on purpose?

00:12:28.490 --> 00:12:33.420
Yeah, artists don't draw 
this much detail these days.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:36.100
They're copycats, but I can't 
tell them to remove the

00:12:36.100 --> 00:12:38.010
shoulder pads after they put 
all that effort into them.

00:12:38.720 --> 00:12:42.480
The heroines didn't seem that 
macho in the initial sketches.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.280
The initial sketches were nothing 
more than a few scribbles.

00:12:45.280 --> 00:12:46.820
Can't make any judgments off that.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:50.250
Oh, so N3016 did the rough sketch,

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:53.030
and N4264 did the outlining.

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:56.590
Yes, since the prison 
didn't allow felt pens.

00:12:57.130 --> 00:12:59.230
Oh, so that's why the submission for the

00:12:59.230 --> 00:13:00.790
Treasure Award was a rough sketch.

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:03.040
Look at his crappy drawings.

00:13:03.260 --> 00:13:06.040
You have no idea how hard it 
was for me to correct this.

00:13:06.040 --> 00:13:07.690
You're headed to the disciplinary room!

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:09.760
You're headed to the disciplinary room!

00:13:07.690 --> 00:13:11.050
Uh, was the pen you used 
covered in mud or something?!

00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:13.990
It's embarrassing, so don't 
compare my art to Bro's!

00:13:13.990 --> 00:13:17.070
They should switch roles!

00:13:17.070 --> 00:13:20.800
And the guy with an ugly 
face can draw some cute art!

00:13:20.800 --> 00:13:23.020
He's made a ton of progress!

00:13:23.020 --> 00:13:25.060
He's a genius, if you 
ignore the shoulder pads!

00:13:25.300 --> 00:13:27.240
I-I understand.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:29.920
Then let's have the two of you swap roles

00:13:29.920 --> 00:13:31.460
on the next submission.

00:13:31.460 --> 00:13:32.290
Huh?!

00:13:32.290 --> 00:13:34.750
Well, it's good now, but I'm

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:36.950
interested in seeing what else you can do.

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:39.780
But I don't know how to use a mapping pen

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:41.800
since I've been a model prisoner!

00:13:41.800 --> 00:13:44.710
Uh, you don't have to use a mapping pen.

00:13:45.110 --> 00:13:47.990
N4264 writes the story

00:13:47.990 --> 00:13:51.000
and N3016 draws a rough sketch off that.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:53.720
Then you just have to fax it to me.

00:13:54.070 --> 00:13:58.640
Seriously?! My art can't 
compare with Bro's!

00:13:58.640 --> 00:14:01.320
No, I guarantee that your art is better.

00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:03.950
Well, this might help him 
realize how hard my job is.

00:14:03.950 --> 00:14:05.580
Sounds like fun. Let's do it.

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:08.030
Why are you so arrogant?!

00:14:08.030 --> 00:14:09.730
You're the one holding back this manga!

00:14:09.730 --> 00:14:13.730
<b>Shueisha</b>

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:13.730
Thank you very much for seeing us today.

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:16.720
We'll fax you our next work, 
so please give us a chance.

00:14:16.720 --> 00:14:18.740
Yes, I'm looking forward to seeing it.

00:14:20.210 --> 00:14:25.250
With that art, and a story 
that lays his own life bare...

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:30.250
There are many obstacles 
ahead, but it's possible that

00:14:31.120 --> 00:14:34.780
I've found an incredible talent.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:45.290
Vanguard-san, you have a fax.

00:14:45.290 --> 00:14:47.350
The gorilla finally finished?

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:50.380
Oh, no. It's from someone 
named Mute Ashirogi.

00:14:47.600 --> 00:14:53.610
<b>Jump Editing Department Mr. Vanguard
We finished our first draft. Please have a look.</b>

00:14:51.840 --> 00:14:53.610
What? It only took them one day?

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:58.120
These newbies are so much 
faster than the gorilla.

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.610
Let's see. What's the title?

00:15:00.840 --> 00:15:02.300
God of Death?

00:15:02.650 --> 00:15:03.940
So they focused on the

00:15:03.940 --> 00:15:06.270
reaper aspect instead of the prison theme.

00:15:06.490 --> 00:15:08.200
Huh? There's more below?

00:15:07.040 --> 00:15:11.290
<b>Prison of Death</b>

00:15:08.600 --> 00:15:10.470
Oh, so it hasn't been finalized.

00:15:10.470 --> 00:15:11.950
Looks like they were shifting between

00:15:11.290 --> 00:15:14.460
<b>Death Prison
Death PriDeath</b>

00:15:11.950 --> 00:15:14.340
the reaper and prison themes.

00:15:14.460 --> 00:15:18.470
<b>PriDeath PriDeath
Death PriPri Death</b>

00:15:14.820 --> 00:15:18.390
Er, I don't like where this is going.

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:23.270
You don't want to start 
mixing and matching words.

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:23.050
<b>Death PriPri Death
PriPriDeath</b>

00:15:23.050 --> 00:15:27.100
<b>CHAGE here.</b>

00:15:23.700 --> 00:15:27.280
This has nothing to do 
with reapers or prisons.

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:29.730
<b>ASKA here.</b>

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:30.090
What happened to the death and pripri?

00:15:29.730 --> 00:15:33.110
<b>CHAGE & ASKA here.</b>

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:33.480
Why is this like the intro 
for a CHAGE & ASKA concert?

00:15:33.110 --> 00:15:35.360
<b>ASKA & CHAGE here.</b>

00:15:33.480 --> 00:15:35.870
Who cares about the order?!

00:15:35.360 --> 00:15:37.860
<b>ASKA & CHAGE & ASKA here.</b>

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:38.540
Don't put CHAGE in between two ASKAs!

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:39.360
<b>ASKA & CHAGE & ASKA here.</b>

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:40.390
Staggering it doesn't help!

00:15:39.360 --> 00:15:41.490
<b>CHAGE DEATH ASKA</b>

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:42.420
Why are you bringing death 
back into the title?!

00:15:41.490 --> 00:15:44.620
<b>CHAGETH NOTE</b>

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.810
And now this is just completely wrong!

00:15:45.810 --> 00:15:47.620
What is this CHAGETH NOTE?

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:48.730
Does something bad happen

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:51.250
